# with the byte at file offset 11250 XORed with 0xFF -- the 6th payload byte
# of models/asset_010.t3dm, and nothing else.
#
# What expectation.json records the reference reader doing: streamdb_emb_get
# returns STREAMDB_EMB_ERR_CRC for that ONE key; the other 23 read back
# byte-exact; the suffix searches are unaffected, since the trie and index
# were not touched.
#
# What this reader must do, and what expected.out (29,988 bytes) holds: the
# container still OPENS -- the index and trie CRCs are intact, so exit is 0 --
# and the stream's section 2 carries verdict 2 (checksum mismatch) with length
# 0 and no payload for models/asset_010.t3dm alone. That document's 2,603
# payload bytes are the WHOLE difference from streamdb_corpus/expected.out --
# 32,591 - 29,988 = 2,603 -- plus the one verdict byte, which changes from 0
# to 2 in place.
#
# THE RECORD HEADER STILL AGREES with the index entry here -- the flip is in
# the payload, so the size and crc at `offset - 8` are unchanged -- which is
# exactly why this case proves the PAYLOAD CRC is computed and not merely the
# header check. The header check is proved by mutant 1 in the commit message.
